#. module: l10n_ca_nu_payroll
#: model:l10n_ca.payroll.source,summary:l10n_ca_nu_payroll.source_t4127_123
msgid ""
"2026 Nunavut brackets and constants KP and basic personal amount. The "
"edition lists Nunavut among the jurisdictions without change on July 1, "
"2026."
msgstr ""

#. module: l10n_ca_nu_payroll
#: model:l10n_ca.payroll.source,summary:l10n_ca_nu_payroll.source_payroll_registration_form
msgid ""
"A withholding or pay-as-you-earn payroll tax of 2% of all gross remuneration"
" paid to the employees who work more than half their time for an employer in"
" Nunavut, collected by the employer from each employee. Registration within "
"21 days after the first remuneration paid."
msgstr ""

#. module: l10n_ca_nu_payroll
#: model:l10n_ca.payroll.source,summary:l10n_ca_nu_payroll.source_wscc_report_payroll
msgid ""
"Annual Payroll Report, the actual payroll of the previous year and an "
"estimate of the current year, due February 28. Directors of a corporation, "
"business owners and the self-employed are not covered automatically; "
"Personal Optional Coverage from 37% of the YMIR up to the YMIR."
msgstr ""

#. module: l10n_ca_nu_payroll
#: model:l10n_ca.payroll.source,summary:l10n_ca_nu_payroll.source_wscc_policy_02_01
msgid ""
"Assessment = (assessable payroll / 100) x the rate of the industry subclass,"
" the payroll of each worker capped at the YMIR; minimum assessment of 200. "
"Payment by March 31, or by instalments of March 31, May 31, July 31 and "
"September 30 for an assessment of 1,000 or more."
msgstr ""

