#. module: l10n_ca_nu_payroll
#: model:l10n_ca.payroll.source,summary:l10n_ca_nu_payroll.source_payroll_guide_2011
msgid ""
"Employers withhold 2% of the gross remuneration of each employee. Not "
"subject: members of religious orders with a vow of poverty, and less than "
"5,000 a year earned in Nunavut by an employee who normally works outside it;"
" withhold once the 5,000 can reasonably be expected to be exceeded. "
"Remittance by the 20th day of the month after the reporting period; annual "
"return, even nil, by February 28."
msgstr ""

#. module: l10n_ca_nu_payroll
#: model:l10n_ca.payroll.source,summary:l10n_ca_nu_payroll.source_payroll_tax_act
msgid ""
"Every employee pays a tax of 2% of the remuneration paid in the year, which "
"the employer withholds. An employee who normally works outside Nunavut owes "
"the tax on the days worked in it, and none on a remuneration of 5,000 or "
"less in the year from the employer (prescribed amount of the regulations). "
"Named Payroll Tax Act, 1993 until 2024."
msgstr ""

